<!--
    The Go boolean-return stale-high artifact (docs/multilang.md W4), ported
    as kuna `option gobool` (P4 output-prototype, default AUTO).

    Go's ABI materializes a bool result as 0/1 in the LOW BYTE of the return
    register and leaves the upper bytes unspecified: the compiler emits a bare
    `SETcc AL` with no zeroing XOR.  kuna faithfully lifts the full-register
    dataflow, so the returned value is PIECE(stale7, bool1) and the C prints

        v = CONCAT71((undefined7)(v >> 8), a0 == 1);
        return v & 0xffffffff;

    SubvariableFlow's return pull rightly refuses to narrow it (nothing proves
    the high bytes zero; rustc never shows the shape because it zeroes first).
    `gobool` rewrites such a RETURN to read ZEXT(bool) - asserting the ABI
    fact the way `rustabi` asserts the ScalarPair - and the dead concatenation
    is collected by ordinary dead-code elimination.

    The bytes are a hand-assembled x86-64 `func isOne(x int) bool` exactly as
    the Go compiler shapes it (a wide definition of the return register
    upstream of the SETcc, so the stale high bytes are real):

        100000  mov  %rdi,%rax        ; RAX written wide (the stale source)
        100003  cmp  $0x1,%rdi
        100007  sete %al              ; bool materialized in the low byte
        10000a  ret

    P0 assertion: `option gobool off|auto|always`.  `auto` (the default) acts
    only on an image whose detected source language is Go; the analyzer tier
    never runs on this bytechunk bootstrap, so the test forces `always`,
    exactly as the `rustabi` and `gomorestack` stage tests force their
    language-blind modes.
    Pass 1 (option gobool off): the artifact - the return is the CONCAT71
      concatenation (assertion #1).
    Pass 2 (option gobool always): the fix - the concatenation is gone and the
      comparison survives as the returned value; #1 stays at exactly one
      occurrence because the second pass contributes none, while the
      comparison (assertion #2) and the `return` (assertion #3) appear once
      per pass.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
4889f84883ff010f94c0c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="is_one"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option gobool off</com>
  <com>lo fu is_one</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option gobool always</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GOBOOL #1: the stale-high concatenation renders under off and narrows under always" min="1" max="1">CONCAT71</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOBOOL #2: the comparison survives both passes" min="2" max="2">a0 == 1</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GOBOOL #3: one return per pass" min="2" max="2">return</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
